🚨 THREAT INTELLIGENCE NOTE — MIEM PAYMENT SYSTEM (URUGUAY)

[TLP:CLEAR · INDEPENDENT OSINT · STATUS: UNVERIFIED]

Actor operating as zfo (DarkForums) claims access to the payment system of the Ministerio de Industria, Energía y Minería. The listing states 10,713 companies, with records allegedly containing company or individual names, Uruguayan RUT or cédula, payment IDs, dates, amounts, status, and form or transaction references. A sample JSON is shown with fields including pago_id, fecha, nombre, rut, importe_total, and estado. The actor also states an intent to offer an API or bot for lookups and frames the activity as part of a broader shift toward Latin American targets.

The same alias has recent DarkForums claims involving Argentine police training records, Mexican tax and customs access, Bolivian student registry data, and collaboration references tied to Dominican civil-registry material. A parallel claim the same day covers a Florida (Uruguay) municipal building-permits dataset. Monitoring sources have logged both as unconfirmed forum reports. No official statement from MIEM, AGESIC, or related payment operators has been located confirming compromise, scope, or data authenticity.

Uruguay’s public systems have faced repeated dark-web claims and confirmed incidents in recent years. Payment records of this type, if genuine, would expose RUT-linked financial activity usable for fraud and targeted phishing. Forum samples and download links alone do not establish system access or data freshness.

DATA OVER DRAMA. Technical claims remain unaudited. No affiliation with any actor, marketplace, or institutional response.

